{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Israel, and under His feet</b> — teaches that they saw the likeness of Jacob beneath the Throne of Glory. And the likeness of their faces was the face of a man. The sefer Torah [reads] תמים, and this is what Jacob said: \"Am I in place of Elohim?\" — אנכי in gematria [equals] כסא." "<b>לבנת</b> — twice in the Masorah: here and the other ובשיחור לבנת in Joshua, and there it is the name of a city, called so after being built of bricks. And this is what they expounded, that it was like a brick, to remember the servitude of Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:15.378591336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}